WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.067 --> 00:00:04.847
AI agents fail in production not because the technology is immature,

2
00:00:04.847 --> 00:00:08.467
but because the patterns for running them are still being invented.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.700
Underneath, running an agent is a distributed systems problem.

4
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.040
When a refund call times out,

5
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.820
the agent retries without checking if the first one landed,

6
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.800
so the refund goes out twice.

7
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.600
Splitting work across agents makes it worse,

8
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.800
because five agents at ninety percent reliability multiply out to fifty-nine percent.

9
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.120
So before adding agents,

10
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:35.120
I'd put in a circuit breaker that halts the loop past an error threshold,

11
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.920
and observability on each tool result.
